  slide "Locust: why overshoot" {
    eyebrow: "Locust architecture"
    title: "No central admission means stopping at N is poll-then-kill"
    lede: "Locust core has no built-in 'stop after N total requests' primitive. Because greenlets fire independently with no admission gate, the only lever to stop at a target is periodic stats polling plus a hard kill — which structurally overshoots and abandons stragglers."

    narration: "This follows directly from the greenlet model, not from any specific script's choices. Every virtual-user greenlet loops and fires its own requests with no per-request check-in against a central authority — there is nothing in the architecture that could tell a single greenlet 'stop now, we've hit N.' The only aggregate view of total completed requests is environment.stats.total, refreshed on the master from a periodic worker_report event that core Locust fires every WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL — a fixed 3.0-second cadence, not driven by request completions. A stop-at-N implementation has no choice but to watch that periodic report and, once the target is crossed, call runner.quit(). And runner.quit()'s own docstring says exactly what it does: stop the test and kill all greenlets. Any request a greenlet was mid-flight on at that instant is simply abandoned, uncounted — there's no drain phase, because there's no per-request admission ledger to drain against, only greenlets to kill or not kill."

    term: {
      word: "poll-then-kill"
      meaning: "The only mechanism available to stop a Locust run at a specific total-request target: periodically check aggregated stats (every WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL, 3.0s) and call runner.quit() once crossed, which kills every greenlet immediately rather than draining in-flight requests — because there is no central admission ledger to drain."
    }

    points: [
      "Locust core has no built-in stop-at-N-requests feature — no primitive to gate admission against a target count.",
      "worker_report fires on a fixed WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL = 3.0s cadence (locust/runners.py), not on request completion.",
      "Stop-at-N is implemented externally: watch worker_report, call runner.quit() once environment.stats.total.num_requests reaches target.",
      "Evidence: locust/runners.py — `WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL = 3.0`; `Runner.quit()` docstring: \"kill all greenlets for the runner\"."
    ]

    caption: "Poll every 3s, then kill — because no credit ledger exists to drain."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s3b-hdr",
        title = "STOP AT N = POLL THEN KILL",
        caption = "Poll every 3s, then kill — because no credit ledger exists to drain.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Stepper(
        id = "s3b-steps",
        steps = ["greenlets fire freely", "poll stats every 3.0s", "target crossed", "quit() kills all"],
        linked = true,
        gap = 14,
        x = 40, y = 74, width = 600, height = 26
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s3b-fire",
        title = "Greenlets",
        detail = "no per-request check-in",
        x = 40, y = 130, width = 160, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s3b-e1",
        mode = "connector",
        from = { nodeId: "s3b-fire", anchor: "e" },
        to = { nodeId: "s3b-poll", anchor: "w" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.tertiary), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s3b-poll",
        title = "worker_report",
        detail = "every 3.0s (fixed)",
        x = 240, y = 130, width = 160, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.tertiary)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s3b-e2",
        mode = "connector",
        from = { nodeId: "s3b-poll", anchor: "e" },
        to = { nodeId: "s3b-cross", anchor: "w" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.warning), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s3b-cross",
        title = "target crossed",
        detail = "num_requests >= N",
        x = 440, y = 130, width = 160, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.warning)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s3b-kill",
