  slide "AIPerf: credit-synchronized dispatch" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "A central coordinator admits every request with a credit"
    lede: "AIPerf's timing_manager decides when the next request may be sent and hands out a credit — an admission token — to a worker over a ZMQ ROUTER-DEALER socket. Workers don't decide their own concurrency; the coordinator does."

    narration: "This is the piece with no equivalent on the Locust side. In Locust, once a greenlet is running, it decides for itself when to fire its next request — there is no central authority approving each request. In AIPerf, request admission is centralized: the timing manager process is the single source of truth for how many requests are currently allowed to be in flight, and it communicates that decision to workers by dispatching a discrete message called a credit over a ZMQ ROUTER socket, matched to each worker's DEALER socket. A worker only sends an HTTP request once it holds a credit for it. That's what makes AIPerf's concurrency model synchronized rather than simulated: the in-flight count is an explicit, centrally-tracked invariant, not an emergent property of how many greenlets happen to be running."

    term: {
      word: "credit"
      meaning: "A discrete admission token issued by AIPerf's timing_manager to a specific worker process over a ZMQ ROUTER-DEALER socket pair, authorizing that worker to send exactly one request. Concurrency is the count of credits currently outstanding, tracked centrally."
    }

    points: [
      "timing_manager is the single source of truth for how many requests may be in flight.",
      "Dispatch is router → worker over the CREDIT_ROUTER ZMQ address; each worker holds a DEALER socket.",
      "A worker sends an HTTP request only once it has received a credit for it — not on its own schedule.",
      "Evidence: aiperf/credit/sticky_router.py — CreditRouterProtocol, `address=CommAddress.CREDIT_ROUTER`."
    ]

    caption: "Concurrency is a centrally-tracked invariant, not an emergent count of running greenlets."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s5-hdr",
        title = "TIMING_MANAGER ISSUES CREDITS",
        caption = "Concurrency is a centrally-tracked invariant, not an emergent count of running greenlets.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s5-tm",
